cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite both the software archive and the related paper."
type: software
title: "2H_Ge: Codes and data for calculations of hexagonal germanium nanowires"
abstract: >-
  Numerical codes, datasets, plotting notebooks and figure exports supporting the
  manuscript "Spin-orbit interaction and g-tensor anisotropy of holes in nanowires
  of hexagonal germanium". The calculations use a ten-band k·p Hamiltonian,
  discretized with Kwant and analysed with Pymablock, to study confined hole states
  in 2H-Ge nanowires: subband structure, g-tensor anisotropy, electric-field-induced
  Stark shifts and Rashba splitting, and the microscopic origin of the Rashba coupling.
